    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures \u2014 including the new `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` acceptance test).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipTier` is derived by `OwnerMapper` as a pure function of the `Owner` entity (GOLD, then the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules). To keep that single source of truth, I persist a household-size snapshot captured at creation, matching the existing `namesakeCount` pattern:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 computes the household size *after this create* (existing members sharing the same last name + address, `+1` for the new owner; `1` when the owner isn't joining a shared household) and stores it on the owner before saving.\n- **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 added `countOwnersInHousehold(lastName, address)`, reusing the existing normalized household-matching logic.\n- **`Owner`** \u2014 new `householdSize` field mapped to a new `household_size` column.\n- **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_size` column (hsqldb, the test DB, uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must be declared).\n- **`OwnerMapper.formatMembershipTier`** \u2014 returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (this generates `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.GOLD`) and updated the field description.\n\nSemantics note: the tier is a per-owner snapshot taken at creation, faithful to the spec's \"3 or more members **after this create**\" \u2014 the third member of a household is GOLD, while owners created when the household was smaller keep their creation-time tier.\n\nSince this isn't a git repo, I made no commits.",
